[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5120742497","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121892#issuecomment-5120742497","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121892","id":5120742497,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMThUYQ","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-29T16:37:00Z","updated_at":"2026-07-29T16:37:00Z","body":"I tested the generated build and it looks great for a first pass! Here are some of the things I noticed:\r\n- I don't see `compact mode` in the project manager anymore; is the PR just based on an older version that doesn't include those changes?\r\n- The touch action panel should have a [top|bottom] fixed position in portrait and automatically switch from [left|right] in landscape to [top|bottom] in portrait when fixed. When floating, the background for the touch action panel should be translucent (~40% opacity)\r\n- The embedded game view doesn't render properly in portrait. Reusing the same layout component, we can create another view that fits within the portrait dimensions, and switch which one we're showing based on the orientation. Open to other suggestions as well.\r\n- Let's bump up the default scale for the editor to make the UI easier to interact with, and let's optimize the layout based on that scale. \r\n  - From a quick testing, a 200% scale (on a Pixel 10 pro fold) is a good target.\r\n  - At the current scale, things are even harder to interact with in portrait given how small they are. For users that are fine with the current scale, a layout optimized for a larger scale should provide them with even more flexibility.\r\n\r\nWith those changes in place, we should look into the idea of automatically switching to distraction-free mode when the device is rotated to portrait in order to make the new portrait support more discoverable. But that can be left to a follow-up PR.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5120742497/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5121974526","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121892#issuecomment-5121974526","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121892","id":5121974526,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMUsg_g","user":{"login":"arkology","id":43543909,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTQzOTA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43543909?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology","html_url":"https://github.com/arkology","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-29T18:31:58Z","updated_at":"2026-07-29T18:32:22Z","body":"> * Improves some editor parts to better resize to small window width.\r\n\r\n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116879, which works and has no issues, as I remember,\r\nAnd\r\n- https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117285, where I need helping hand to do it properly/finish it.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5121974526/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5122165667","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121892#issuecomment-5122165667","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121892","id":5122165667,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMU4Low","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-29T18:49:05Z","updated_at":"2026-07-29T18:51:24Z","body":"> > * Improves some editor parts to better resize to small window width.\r\n> \r\n> * [Improve `CanvasItemEditor` and `Node3DEditor` minimum size #116879](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116879), which works and has no issues, as I remember,\r\n\r\nSorry, I hadn't seen your PR.\r\nI've also has similar fix but instead of 2 (as you did in your PR) I split it into 3–4 containers to avoid the below situation, i.e there's still alot of space in first row. It could probably be split even further, but there's ongoing work (https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121080 and https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121065) to improve these toolbars, so that refactoring can be done as part of that effort (if this one merges first)\r\n<img width=\"489\" height=\"73\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/23d11ccf-f1c4-443a-b72b-707b18c65f4d\" />\r\n\r\nI guess this PR supersedes that now?\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5122165667/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5122407559","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121892#issuecomment-5122407559","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121892","id":5122407559,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMVG8hw","user":{"login":"arkology","id":43543909,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzNTQzOTA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43543909?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology","html_url":"https://github.com/arkology","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-29T19:13:49Z","updated_at":"2026-07-29T19:13:49Z","body":"To be honest, I don't think we need that many containers. Originally I tried to make 4+ containers, but ended up with 2. This is really subjective anyway.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5122407559/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5136874803","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121892#issuecomment-5136874803","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121892","id":5136874803,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMi59Mw","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-30T22:22:47Z","updated_at":"2026-08-02T08:19:39Z","body":"> I tested the generated build and it looks great for a first pass! Here are some of the things I noticed:\r\n> \r\n> * I don't see `compact mode` in the project manager anymore; is the PR just based on an older version that doesn't include those changes?\r\n\r\nIt was few days old, but I think those changes were in this branch. Anyways, I've rebased it to latest now.\r\n\r\n> * The touch action panel should have a [top|bottom] fixed position in portrait and automatically switch from [left|right] in landscape to [top|bottom] in portrait when fixed. When floating, the background for the touch action panel should be translucent (~40% opacity)\r\n\r\nThe panel won't fit in portrait width. We can add a ScrollContainer but that would also add scroll bars which won't look good. We can revisit this after we have improved touch scrolling.\r\nI've come up with this solution to prevent the panel from taking up width in portrait mode: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121957\r\nAs for making panel translucent, I think that won't help much. I tried but didn't really liked the result :-)\r\n\r\n> * The embedded game view doesn't render properly in portrait. Reusing the same layout component, we can create another view that fits within the portrait dimensions, and switch which one we're showing based on the orientation. Open to other suggestions as well.\r\n\r\nI think we can use game window's \"move/resize\" logic to manually resize the window when orientation changes.\r\n\r\n> * Let's bump up the default scale for the editor to make the UI easier to interact with, and let's optimize the layout based on that scale.\r\n>   \r\n>   * From a quick testing, a 200% scale (on a Pixel 10 pro fold) is a good target.\r\n>   * At the current scale, things are even harder to interact with in portrait given how small they are. For users that are fine with the current scale, a layout optimized for a larger scale should provide them with even more flexibility.\r\n\r\n`auto scale` is already 180% on my device. 200% is also usable (except few places where UI is tightly packed). Looking into it.\r\n~Note: You might be seeing smaller scale (you had previously mentioned 168%) due to navigation bar, try switching to fullscreen and restart.~ It turned out that even with fullscreen enabled, navigation bar is still accounted for in the scale calculation because that happens before we hide the navigation bar.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5136874803/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5156469386","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121892#issuecomment-5156469386","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121892","id":5156469386,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABM1l6ig","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-02T08:15:06Z","updated_at":"2026-08-02T08:23:40Z","body":"@m4gr3d Could you test again?\r\n- Compact mode should be working again in project manager.\r\n- Fixed Android Game window orientation handling.\r\n- There's now a 5% increase in scale. It can be increased a bit more, but considering that we're already seeing cutoffs in a few areas, I think we should go with smaller increases from time to time.\r\n- Created seperate PR (https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121957) for TouchActionsPanel improvements.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5156469386/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5186039109","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121892#issuecomment-5186039109","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121892","id":5186039109,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNRytRQ","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-05T00:15:32Z","updated_at":"2026-08-05T00:16:35Z","body":"> * Compact mode should be working again in project manager.\r\n\r\nThe issue with compact mode is still there. However it only occurs when the project manager is empty (e.g. after uninstalling and reinstalling the app, or clearing the app storage in the Android Settings)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/17e251de-a734-414c-b1c7-859de47ee01d\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5186039109/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5186185298","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121892#issuecomment-5186185298","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121892","id":5186185298,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNR7oUg","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-05T00:39:29Z","updated_at":"2026-08-05T00:39:29Z","body":"> * There's now a 5% increase in scale. It can be increased a bit more, but considering that we're already seeing cutoffs in a few areas, I think we should go with smaller increases from time to time.\r\n\r\nI see you've updated the `DEFAULT_WINDOW_HEIGHT` and `DEFAULT_WINDOW_WIDTH` which updates the default width and height scale; what about the `screen_scale` value retrieved from `godot_io_java->get_scaled_density()`?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5186185298/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5186958687","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121892#issuecomment-5186958687","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121892","id":5186958687,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNSq1Xw","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-05T02:49:29Z","updated_at":"2026-08-05T02:49:29Z","body":"> > * There's now a 5% increase in scale. It can be increased a bit more, but considering that we're already seeing cutoffs in a few areas, I think we should go with smaller increases from time to time.\r\n> \r\n> I see you've updated the `DEFAULT_WINDOW_HEIGHT` and `DEFAULT_WINDOW_WIDTH` which updates the default width and height scale; what about the `screen_scale` value retrieved from `godot_io_java->get_scaled_density()`?\r\n\r\n`screen_scale` is the ideal scale, (It'd be 2.0 on most smartphones, 200% scale). So, I guess it makes sense to keep it as is for now? Goal with the `auto scale` isn't to give users the maximum scale but an ideal scale and then they can increase it or decrease from editor settings.\r\n\r\nSide note: We also shouldn't do drastic changes to `screen_get_scale` method because it's a DisplayServer API and users might be also using it to calculate auto scale and have a tightly packed UI.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5186958687/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5188076367","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121892#issuecomment-5188076367","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121892","id":5188076367,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNTvDTw","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-05T05:50:25Z","updated_at":"2026-08-05T05:50:25Z","body":"> `screen_scale` is the ideal scale, (It'd be 2.0 on most smartphones, 200% scale).\r\n\r\nThe 5% increase looks good, so let's keep that as the default. But for our own testing and UX optimization, let's (manually) use the _ideal scale (200%)_; the goal being, if the updated UX can fit the _ideal scale_, then it'll fit the default scale as well.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5188076367/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_